    seed_jit_f64_option_some_print_sink_reads_raw_payload_as_value_2026-11-27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T21:21:01Z, 2026-11-27T21:21:01Z, open, "wave10"

    seed_jit_f64_option_some_print_sink_reads_raw_payload_as_value_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: reproduced (print c printed Option::Some(0.000...014354639028913) - the enum heap address bit-cast; interpolation printed Option::Some(<enum@0x...>); interpreter oracle Option::Some(0.1)). Root cause: typed float optionals escape float_option_inline.rs to the sinks as one-word forms, but rt_opt_f64_to_string unconditionally did f64::from_bits(raw); interpolation holes route through the type-erased rt_opt_value_to_string which cannot be fixed erased (raw float aliases every tag pattern while i64?/bool? payloads are genuinely tagged). Fix (landed): io_print.rs rt_opt_f64_to_string routes Option-enum words through rt_option_float_bits + rt_is_none, decodes flat boxed-float words, keeps verbatim-bit raw path; NEW typed sink rt_opt_f64_value_to_string + symbol registration across runtime/codegen/elf. Runtime tests f64_option_print_sink 2/2; primitive_option_parity_jit 9/9. Spec f64_option_some_print_sink (SIMPLE_BINARY convention): print example + direct typed interpolation sink GREEN (exact oracles all forms); the generic {c} hole example RED by design (@tag:in-development) until the lowering hunk lands. PENDING HUNK (design at doc/07_guide/compiler/seed_jit_f64_option_some_print_sink_reverification.md): in lowering_expr_builtin.rs rt_value_to_string flat-optional branch route inner F32/F64 to rt_opt_f64_value_to_string. Residuals: i64?/bool? enum-word print/interp sinks share the defect class (separate sinks/owners); nil vs None word indistinguishable. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/language/f64_option_some_print_sink_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler_rust/runtime/tests/f64_option_print_sink.rs"
